 with a single edge in $T$.","A spanning tree may have at most $n-1$ edges, and edge $n$ must close a cycle.","$T$ already contains a path from $u$ to $v$, and $e$ closes it into a cycle."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dc6da628b85fd5e59400527b","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_spanning_tree_91280e83_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A connected undirected network has 7 vertices and 12 edges. To obtain a spanning tree, some edges are removed. How many edges must be removed?","options":["5 edges, leaving 7, one edge for each vertex","7 edges, one for each vertex of the network","6 edges, leaving the 6 that a tree on 7 vertices has","11 edges, keeping a single edge between two vertices"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b877520fb7fa83cc75f42137","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_spanning_tree_91280e83_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"A spanning tree has the edges 1–2, 2–3, 3–4, 2–5, 5–6, 3–7. The original edge 4–6 is added. Which tree edge must then be removed to obtain a new spanning tree that contains 4–6?","options":["The edge 1–2","The edge 3–7","The edge 2–5","No edge, since 4–6 keeps it a tree"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5e53a738430836a6a03e1a1b","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"}]}}